From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: drain responses before freeing session context

Keep borrowed instance pointers alive through each HFI packet dispatch.
Serialize both generation dispatch paths against registry removal with a
core response mutex. Assert the borrowed-pointer contract at lookup and
require removal to drop the instance lock before waiting for a dispatcher.

Stop capture/output queues without freeing them, preserving the existing
mem2mem release stop order. Permit stop and close completions to run, then
drain old response users and detach the instance before releasing controls,
mem2mem queues, file handles, formats or instance memory. Do not hold the
response mutex during waits or CPU/DMA allocator cleanup. Report the first
streamoff API error without skipping the other queue stop.

OEM Venus has a different session-destroy lifetime. OnePlus Iris33 owns
instances with krefs and additional workqueues; its complete lifecycle is
not portable here. The upstream Iris lookup has three synchronous packet
consumers, so protect their borrowed pointer scope without a new deferred
release worker or donor board policy. Native matching remains disabled.

This establishes CPU response/context lifetime only. A successful framework
cancellation is not proof of firmware DMA quiescence. Session-close timeout
ownership, failed-stop recovery, full platform removal, exported DMA-BUFs
and DMA-domain lifetime remain separate activation gates.

